WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.127
There are many advanced retrieval techniques, but they should solve specific problems.

00:00:05.127 --> 00:00:10.702
Multi-query retrieval creates several alternative searches for one question.

00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:16.692
HyDE generates a hypothetical answer and embeds that instead of the short question.

00:00:16.692 --> 00:00:22.822
Parent-child retrieval searches small chunks but returns a larger surrounding section.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:28.287
Context compression reduces the amount of retrieved text before generation.

00:00:28.287 --> 00:00:34.990
These methods can be useful, but each one adds complexity, latency, and new failure modes.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.627
The best workflow is to begin with a strong baseline and an evaluation set.

00:00:40.627 --> 00:00:46.667
Identify a real failure. Then choose one method that could address that failure.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:50.162
Run the same evaluation again and compare.

00:00:50.162 --> 00:00:55.557
Do not build a complicated RAG stack simply because a technique is popular.

00:00:55.557 --> 00:01:02.748
A simple, measurable system is often more useful than a complex system that nobody understands.
